{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22787 - PROTEIN:4923",
  "verbalization": "Khrinone C is shown to interact with CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a target of multiple compounds, including (1S,3E,4S,5S,6S)-4,5-dihydroxy-3-(3-methylbut-2-enylidene)-7-oxabicyclo[4.1.0]heptan-2-one, (1R,2S,4S,5R,8S,9R,12S,13R,14S)-1-hydroxy-14-(2-hydroxypropan-2-yl)-13-methyl-3,7,10-trioxapentacyclo[6.4.1.19,12.02,4.05,13]tetradecane-6,11-dione, and (+)-(5S,7R)-7-Ethoxy-12-Hydroxy-2-Oxo-20-Norabieta-1(10),8,11,13-Tetraene. All these compounds share a common mechanism of targeting the sialyltransferase enzyme, which is critical for the synthesis of sialic acid. This suggests that Khrinone C may exert its effects through a similar mechanism, possibly by modulating the sialyltransferase activity. The evidence supports a potential role for Khrinone C in influencing Neuropilin-2 through its interaction with this enzyme, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
